162
00:08:23,450 --> 00:08:26,370
For case number three, we
have a female infant that

163
00:08:26,370 --> 00:08:29,150
is born full-term via
spontaneous vaginal delivery

164
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:31,690
to a mother who recently
immigrated from India.

165
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:33,990
No prenatal records
are available.

166
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:37,930
During the initial newborn
exam, you note that the

167
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:41,410
child is small for
gestational age, has a heart

168
00:08:41,410 --> 00:08:45,010
murmur, hepatosplenomegaly,
and a papular bluish rash.

169
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:51,630
Here is the child and
the rash that is noted.

170
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:56,070
The illness in this
infant could have been

171
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:58,150
prevented by which of
the following measures?

172
00:09:00,610 --> 00:09:03,290
The answer here
is A, immunization

173
00:09:03,290 --> 00:09:04,990
of the mother
prior to pregnancy.

174
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:09,190
This is a case of
congenital rubella syndrome.

175
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:13,030
In our case, the
newborn presented with a

176
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:16,490
blueberry muffin rash or
dermal erythral poiesis.

177
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:19,670
The newborn also
had a murmur, which

178
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,230
could have been due
to a patent ductus

179
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:24,150
arteriosus or
pulmonic stenosis.

180
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:27,330
The newborn also had
hepatospenomegaly,

181
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:28,930
which would likely
lead to jaundice

182
00:09:28,930 --> 00:09:30,910
in the first day
or two of life.

183
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:34,190
The infection can also cause

184
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:37,110
cataracts,
retinopathy, glaucoma,

185
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:40,290
sensory neural
hearing loss, a growth

186
00:09:40,290 --> 00:09:42,290
