with an exanthem that

528
00:28:18,210 --> 00:28:21,510
is characterized by a
herald patch. This is where

529
00:28:21,510 --> 00:28:24,310
you have a single 3 to
5 centimeter isolated

530
00:28:24,310 --> 00:28:28,010
oval scaly pink patch
with central clearing.

531
00:28:28,130 --> 00:28:30,970
And then additional
lesions will develop over

532
00:28:30,970 --> 00:28:33,790
the following one to
two weeks. These lesions

533
00:28:33,790 --> 00:28:36,570
will be very peritic,
scaly, and erythematous

534
00:28:36,570 --> 00:28:39,930
plaques that often have
a choleret of scale.

535
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:43,390
A buzzword that you
might see in terms of the

536
00:28:43,390 --> 00:28:45,890
pattern of these lesions
is called a Christmas

537
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:49,010
tree pattern. The
spread is cephalocaudal.

538
00:28:49,270 --> 00:28:51,390
Your diagnosis is clinical,

539
00:28:51,590 --> 00:28:55,310
but if you are considering
tinea or ******** on your

540
00:28:55,310 --> 00:28:57,910
differential, you can do
testing to exclude those.

541
00:28:58,250 --> 00:28:59,830
Treatment is supportive.

542
00:29:00,170 --> 00:29:01,930
Specifically, though,
you might recommend an

543
00:29:01,930 --> 00:29:04,550
antihistamine or a topical
steroid for the itching.

544
00:29:05,870 --> 00:29:07,490
Pitoriasis rosea will resolve

545
00:29:07,490 --> 00:29:10,270
spontaneously after
six to eight weeks.

